From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: j7prime p3 <p3@j7prime.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos7870-on7xelte: use the SD card-detect GPIO

The SD slot is described with broken-cd, so the MMC core polls it every
second, switching its two regulators on and off each time (about 100
interrupts/s on the host plus PMIC i2c traffic, measured idle). gpa0-1
is already in the slot's pinctrl group as an EINT pin; use it as the
card-detect GPIO instead.

The polarity is not verified (no card to test with): if it is wrong the
slot sees a card when there is none and fails one initialisation; it
does not poll either way.

Origin: new in j7prime p3.
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---

Notes:
    New.

 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
@@ -935,7 +935,14 @@
 	samsung,dw-mshc-ddr-timing = <1 2>;
 	sd-uhs-sdr50;
 	sd-uhs-sdr104;
-	broken-cd;
+	/*
+	 * gpa0-1 is the card-detect line (already in pinctrl-0 as an EINT
+	 * pin). Without it the slot was polled every second (broken-cd),
+	 * power-cycling its regulators each time. Polarity not verified:
+	 * if inverted, the slot sees a card when there is none (one failed
+	 * init at boot, no polling either way).
+	 */
+	cd-gpios = <&gpa0 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	disable-wp;
 
 	status = "okay";
-- 
